    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Unleash ops agent in Slack (Enterprise)\n\nMention the bot in Slack to ask things like \"what changed in production today?\", and it can roll out a flag on request. The agent picks which Unleash MCP tool to call per message, instead of running one fixed call.\n\n**Requires Unleash Enterprise** — the MCP server is Enterprise-only. [Start a trial](https://www.getunleash.io/plans/enterprise-payg).\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Create a Slack app with an Events API subscription for `app_mention`, and connect your Slack credential here.\n2. Turn on the Remote MCP Server under Admin in your Unleash instance, and connect a Bearer personal access token credential to the MCP tool node.\n3. Connect your own Chat Model credential (OpenAI shown here — swap for any model the AI Agent node supports).\n\nTools given to the agent are limited to **search, inspect, evaluate, release, docs** — the read-only and rollout tools, not `kill_switch`, `manage_flag`, `configure`, `experiment` or `audit`. Add those explicitly if you want the agent to do more; `release` already opens a change request wherever the environment requires one, so this won't bypass approvals.\n\nThe reply step assumes the Slack trigger's output has a `channel` field — verify that against a real event from your workspace and adjust the expression if your payload differs; this hasn't been run against a live Slack app in this repo.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 480
      },
